casebook d-30cfr-75_1103-5-mine-co-warning-draft v1
source "D-30cfr-75.1103-5-mine-co-warning.txt" dated 2026-10-14 by "drafted by anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 from the manual; not yet approved"
note "UNAPPROVED DRAFT: written by a language model from D-30cfr-75.1103-5-mine-co-warning.txt. Every declaration below cites the sentence"
note "it came from. Check each against the manual, add what the manual does not say, then delete"
note "this note to approve. quorum studio will not build a chip image while it is here."

# manual: "When the carbon monoxide level reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level at any sensor location"
observe co_high "carbon monoxide is 10 ppm above the established ambient level at a sensor location"

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning"
observe sensor_warning "a sensor indicates a warning"

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
observe operator_no_hazard "the mine operator has determined the signal does not present a hazard to miners"

# manual: "If any fire detection component becomes inoperative, immediate action must be taken to repair the component."
observe detector_inoperative "a fire detection component has become inoperative"

# manual: "of any change in this information"
observe map_info_changed "the sensor locations or intended air flow direction shown on the map or schematic have changed"

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours"
observe map_updated "the map or schematic has been updated within 24 hours of the change"

# manual: "after the belt is stopped"
observe belt_stopped_recently "the belt has been stopped and the 4-hour period after stopping has not yet ended"

# manual: "an examination for hot rollers and fire is made"
observe hot_roller_exam_made "an examination for hot rollers and fire has been made"

# manual: "When a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location"
observe surface_signal_received "a malfunction or warning signal has been received at the manned surface location"

# manual: "Upon notification of a malfunction or warning signal"
observe notified_of_signal "personnel have been notified of a malfunction or warning signal"

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
observe assigned_emergency_duties "the miners are assigned emergency response duties"

# manual: "If the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors"
observe calibration_warning_expected "the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors"

# manual: "If two or more adjacent sensors become inoperative"
observe adjacent_sensors_inoperative "two or more adjacent sensors have become inoperative"

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative"
observe complete_system_inoperative "the complete fire detection system has become inoperative"

# manual: "any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
observe monitor_co_high "a trained person monitoring finds carbon monoxide 10 ppm above the established ambient level"

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
observe source_known_harmless "the mine operator knows the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"

# manual: "during calibration of sensors"
observe calibrating "calibration of sensors is in progress"

# manual: "If one sensor becomes inoperative"
observe one_sensor_inoperative "one sensor has become inoperative"

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
excuse operator_judgement "the operator has determined the signal is not a hazard to miners" needs operator_no_hazard

# manual: "When the carbon monoxide level reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level at any sensor location, automatic fire sensor and warning device systems shall provide an effective warning signal at the following locations"
claim fire_warning "carbon monoxide 10 ppm above ambient at a sensor requires an effective warning signal" severity 5 needs co_high

# manual: "If any fire detection component becomes inoperative, immediate action must be taken to repair the component."
claim detector_down "a fire detection component is inoperative and needs repair and manual monitoring" severity 4 needs detector_inoperative

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning, the following actions must be taken"
claim hazard_warning "a sensor warning requires the listed actions, including withdrawing miners from the affected areas" severity 8 needs sensor_warning

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
claim map_out_of_date "the map or schematic has not been updated after a change in the information it shows" severity 2 needs map_info_changed

# manual: "shall be monitored for a period of 4 hours after the belt is stopped"
claim monitoring_required "the fire sensor and warning device system must be monitored for 4 hours after the belt is stopped" severity 3 needs belt_stopped_recently

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made"
excuse examination_instead "an examination for hot rollers and fire has been made, so the 4-hour monitoring is not required" needs hot_roller_exam_made

# manual: "appropriate personnel must immediately initiate an investigation to determine the cause of the malfunction or warning signal"
claim investigation_due "after notification of a malfunction or warning signal, an investigation into its cause must be started immediately" severity 4 needs notified_of_signal

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
excuse emergency_response_duty "miners assigned emergency response duties are not withdrawn" needs assigned_emergency_duties

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
claim report_to_surface_due "monitoring persons must immediately report carbon monoxide 10 ppm above ambient to the surface" severity 5 needs monitor_co_high

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
excuse harmless_source_known "the operator knows the carbon monoxide source is not a hazard, so no immediate report is required" needs source_known_harmless

# manual: "Affected working sections, areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, or other areas designated in the approved emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration."
claim calibration_area_notice_due "calibration of sensors is under way, so affected working sections and designated areas must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration" severity 3 needs calibrating

# manual: "When a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location"
claim notification_due "a signal received at the manned surface location requires the activated sensors to be identified and appropriate personnel notified immediately" severity 4 needs surface_signal_received

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning, the following actions must be taken"
claim notify_miners_due "a sensor warning requires miners in affected sections and areas to be notified unless the operator finds no hazard" severity 7 needs sensor_warning

# manual: "If the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors"
claim calibration_notice_due "calibration will activate the warning signal, so personnel manning the surface location must be notified before and after calibration" severity 3 needs calibration_warning_expected

# manual: "If two or more adjacent sensors become inoperative"
claim adjacent_sensors_down "two or more adjacent sensors are inoperative, so the affected areas must be patrolled and monitored" severity 4 needs adjacent_sensors_inoperative

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative"
claim complete_system_down "the complete fire detection system is inoperative, so the affected areas must be patrolled and monitored" severity 4 needs complete_system_inoperative

# manual: "If one sensor becomes inoperative"
claim one_sensor_down "one sensor is inoperative, so a trained person must monitor at that sensor" severity 4 needs one_sensor_inoperative

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
operator_judgement undercuts hazard_warning

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours"
map_updated rebuts map_out_of_date

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made"
examination_instead undercuts monitoring_required

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
operator_judgement undercuts notify_miners_due

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
emergency_response_duty undercuts hazard_warning

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
harmless_source_known undercuts report_to_surface_due

# manual: "must be immediately withdrawn to a safe location identified in the mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction"
action withdraw_miners safe when any hazard_warning

# manual: "shall provide an effective warning signal"
action raise_alarm when any fire_warning

# manual: "operation of the belt may continue"
action keep_running idle

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
action update_map when any map_out_of_date

# manual: "shall be monitored for a period of 4 hours after the belt is stopped"
action monitor_system when any monitoring_required

# manual: "the sensors that are activated must be identified and appropriate personnel immediately notified"
action notify_personnel when any notification_due

# manual: "appropriate personnel must immediately initiate an investigation to determine the cause of the malfunction or warning signal"
action investigate_cause when any investigation_due

# manual: "Appropriate personnel must notify miners in affected working sections, in affected areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, and at other locations specified in the approved mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction"
action notify_miners when any notify_miners_due

# manual: "personnel manning the surface location must be notified prior to and upon completion of calibration"
action notify_surface_personnel when any calibration_notice_due

# manual: "must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration"
action notify_calibration_areas when any calibration_area_notice_due

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
action patrol_affected_areas when any adjacent_sensors_down

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
action patrol_all_areas when any complete_system_down

# manual: "must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
action report_to_surface when any report_to_surface_due

# manual: "a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
action monitor_manually when any one_sensor_down

# manual: "immediate action must be taken to repair the component"
action repair_component when any detector_down

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
prefer withdraw_miners over notify_miners over raise_alarm over report_to_surface over notify_personnel over notify_surface_personnel over notify_calibration_areas over investigate_cause over repair_component over patrol_all_areas over patrol_affected_areas over monitor_manually over monitor_system over update_map over keep_running
